PKGMAN-UNLOCK(8) "@PACKAGE_STRING@"

# NAME

pkgman-unlock - unlock packages for updates

# SYNOPSIS

*pkgman unlock* _package-name_ ...

# DESCRIPTION

The *pkgman unlock* command unlocks the specified packages, allowing
them to be updated by *pkgman-sysup*(8) or *pkgman-update*(8).

# FILES

_@SHAREDSTATEDIR@/pkg/locked_
	Database of locked packages.

# EXIT STATUS

*0*
	Packages unlocked successfully.
*>0*
	One or more packages were not found, unlocked, or an error
	occurred.

# SEE ALSO

*pkgman-lock*(8),
*pkgman-list-locked*(1),
*pkgman-sysup*(8),
*pkgman-update*(8),
*pkgman*(1),
*pkgman.conf*(5)

# REPORTING BUGS

Report bugs to: @PACKAGE_BUGREPORT@++
Project homepage: @PACKAGE_URL@

